                <a href="/blog/yoga-alliance-certification">Certification</a>
                <a href="/blog/lagos-travel-guide-ytt-students">Lagos Guide</a>
                <a href="/instructors">Instructors</a>
            </div>
            <a href="#apply" class="nav-cta">Apply Now</a>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <section class="hero">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="badge">Yoga Alliance Certified — RYT200</div>
            <h1>200-Hour Yoga Teacher Training <span class="highlight">Portugal</span></h1>
            <p class="hero-subtitle">Lagos, Algarve — September 2026 | 60 hours online + 15-day immersive intensive on Praia da Batata beach</p>
            <div class="cta-group">
                <a href="#apply" class="btn-primary">Apply Now — Early Bird €1,490</a>
                <a href="/blog/cost-of-yoga-teacher-training-portugal" class="btn-secondary">Compare Costs</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    
    <div class="trust-bar">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="trust-items">
                <div class="trust-item"><span class="icon">✓</span> Yoga Alliance Accredited</div>
                <div class="trust-item"><span class="icon">✓</span> 15+ Years Each Instructor</div>
                <div class="trust-item"><span class="icon">✓</span> 3 Payment Installments</div>
                <div class="trust-item"><span class="icon">✓</span> Limited to 15 Students</div>
                <div class="trust-item"><span class="icon">✓</span> Beachfront Training Location</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="features">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Why Train in Portugal?</h2>
            <div class="features-grid">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">🏝</div>
                    <h3>Train Where Others Vacation</h3>
                    <p>Heat Lagos sits across from <a href="https://yogateachertrainingportugal.eu/blog/lagos-travel-guide-ytt-students">Praia da Batata</a>, minutes from Meia Praia. Theory sessions happen outside — on the sand, in the Portuguese sun. <a href="/blog/best-yoga-teacher-training-portugal">See why Portugal leads European YTT destinations</a>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">👥</div>
                    <h3>Expert Trainers</h3>
                    <p>Led by <a href="/instructors">Stine and Sebastian</a> — each with 15+ years of practice and teaching. You get two perspectives, two teaching styles, and decades of real-world experience.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">📚</div>
                    <h3>Modern Curriculum</h3>
                    <p>We honour yoga's depth while translating it into language that resonates with modern life. Plus honest, practical training on the business of yoga — freelancing, retreats, studio work.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">🤝</div>
                    <h3>Real Community</h3>
                    <p>Intentionally limited to 15 participants. This isn't a factory. You'll leave genuinely transformed — more confident in your voice, clearer as a teacher, and connected to a real community.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="instructors">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Your Instructors</h2>
            <p class="instructors-subtitle">15+ years each. Two teaching styles. One shared mission.</p>
            <div class="instructors-grid">
                <div class="instructor-card">
                    <h3>Stine</h3>
                    <div class="role">Lead Instructor — Vinyasa & Yoga Philosophy</div>
                    <p>Stine has spent 15+ years immersed in Vinyasa practice, teaching across Europe and developing a sequencing methodology that balances creative freedom with anatomical safety. Her classes are known for intelligent progressions and the ability to make complex poses accessible.</p>
                    <p>She's certified at the 500-hour level through Yoga Alliance and has trained extensively in hands-on adjustments, trauma-informed teaching, and yoga for athletes.</p>
                    <div class="credentials">
                        <span>Credentials:</span> E-RYT 500, Yoga Alliance Certified, 15+ Years Teaching, Specialization in Vinyasa Sequencing & Hands-On Adjustments
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="instructor-card">
                    <h3>Sebastian</h3>
                    <div class="role">Lead Instructor — Teaching Methodology & Business of Yoga</div>
                    <p>Sebastian brings 15+ years of yoga practice combined with a background in business and martial arts (BJJ black belt). His unique angle: teaching yoga teachers how to build sustainable careers — not just how to lead a class.</p>
                    <p>He's built multiple wellness businesses and understands the practical realities of freelancing, retreat hosting, studio management, and online teaching. His methodology section is where most graduates say they got their most valuable insights.</p>
                    <div class="credentials">
                        <span>Credentials:</span> RYT 200, 15+ Years Practice, BJJ Black Belt, Business Owner — Heat Lagos, Specialist in Yoga Entrepreneurship & Teaching Methodology
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="details-grid">
                <div class="detail-item">
                    <h4>Dates</h4>
                    <p>Sept 27 — Oct 12, 2026</p>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-item">
                    <h4>Format</h4>
                    <p>60h Online + 15-Day</p>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-item">
                    <h4>Investment</h4>
                    <p class="price">€1,490</p>
                    <p class="installment">Early bird | 3 instalments</p>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-item">
                    <h4>Payment</h4>
                    <p>3 Instalments</p>
                    <p class="installment">€500 + €500 + €490</p>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-item">
                    <h4>Certification</h4>
                    <p>Yoga Alliance RYT200</p>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-item">
                    <h4>Group Size</h4>
                    <p>Limited to 15</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="curriculum">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>What You Will Learn</h2>
            <div class="curriculum-grid">
                <div class="curriculum-item">
                    <h3>Intelligent Sequencing</h3>
                    <p>Theme-based classes: backbends, inversions, arm balances. Progressive peak pose building that creates transformative experiences.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="curriculum-item">
                    <h3>Multiple Styles</h3>
                    <p>Slow Flow and Yang Yin styles. Smart progressions, regressions, and hands-on adjustments for every body.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="curriculum-item">
                    <h3>Teach With Confidence</h3>
                    <p>How to read a room and teach authentic, full-length classes from day one — not just theory, but real practice.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="curriculum-item">
                    <h3>Modern Philosophy</h3>
                    <p>Honour the depth and history of yoga while making it relevant for athletes, professionals, and busy modern lives.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="curriculum-item">
                    <h3>Business of Yoga</h3>
                    <p>Freelancing, studio work, retreats, and building a sustainable teaching career. Most 200-hour trainings skip this. We don't.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="curriculum-item">
                    <h3>Supportive Environment</h3>
                    <p>Serious work balanced with play, laughter, experimentation, and connection. How people actually learn best.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="location-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Where You'll Train</h2>
            <p class="subtitle">Heat Lagos — directly across from Praia da Batata, Lagos' most popular beach</p>
            <div class="location-grid">
                <div class="location-info">
                    <h3>The Studio</h3>
                    <p>Heat Lagos is located in the heart of Lagos, directly across from Praia da Batata — the beach that draws the most foot traffic in the Algarve. The studio features 30-32°C infrared heating technology that warms your body and the floor, not the air. You sweat, you stretch, you breathe.</p>
                    <p>Many of our theory sessions take place outside on the sand, in the Portuguese sun. This isn't a classroom — it's a beachfront learning environment.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>30-32°C infrared heat (not overwhelming 40°C Bikram)</li>
                        <li>Steps from Praia da Batata and Meia Praia</li>
                        <li>Old Town Lagos within walking distance</li>
                        <li>300+ sunny days per year</li>
                        <li>Surf breaks nearby for morning sessions</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="address">
                        <p class="label">Address</p>
                        <p>Edificio da Fabrica da Ribeira</p>
                        <p>Av. dos Descobrimentos, Loja G</p>
                        <p>8600-854 Lagos, Portugal</p>
                        <p style="margin-top:10px"><a href="https://heatlagos.com" target="_blank" style="color:#00d4aa">Visit Heat Lagos →</a></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="location-info">
                    <h3>Why Lagos for YTT?</h3>
                    <p>Lagos combines reliable Algarve sunshine with a laid-back atmosphere that supports deep learning. Unlike busier resort towns, Lagos has retained its character — cobblestone streets, fresh seafood, and a community that welcomes visitors.</p>
                    <p>For your training, this means:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Affordable accommodation:</strong> Airbnbs from €40/night near the beach</li>
                        <li><strong>World-class food:</strong> Fresh seafood, local markets, international options</li>
                        <li><strong>Easy transport:</strong> Faro airport 45 min, Lisbon 3 hours</li>
                        <li><strong>Activities:</strong> Surf, paddleboard, cliff walks, beach yoga</li>
                        <li><strong>Community:</strong> English-speaking expat and yoga community</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="margin-top:20px"><a href="/blog/lagos-travel-guide-ytt-students" class="btn-tertiary">Full Lagos Travel Guide →</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

